menu "Power measurement"

config APP_PAUSE_NOISE_TIMER
    bool "Pause RF noise timer while AP is off"
    default y
    help
        Pause only the SDK noise timer after RF shutdown, block rearming while
        paused, and restore it before AP startup. Ignore a stale FRC2 alarm
        only when the actual SDK timer queue is empty; keep FRC2 counting.
        Build-local library copies expose timer objects without fixed RAM
        addresses. Unsupported SDK object layouts fail configuration.

config APP_PAUSE_NETWORK_TIMERS
    bool "Pause lwIP cyclic/TCP timers while AP is off"
    default y
    help
        Pause protocol cyclic timers and the on-demand TCP timer only after
        networking has stopped. Restore them before starting the AP. Timer
        list changes run synchronously in the TCP/IP thread. Other SDK and
        application timers remain active. Disable and rebuild to compare.

config APP_DISABLE_DHCP_CLIENT_TIMERS
    bool "Disable DHCP client cyclic timers (AP-only A/B test)"
    default y
    help
        Remove the DHCP client fine/coarse cyclic timer entries at build time.
        Keep DHCP server timers and client API symbols for SDK compatibility.
        This application supports AP only; disable this option before adding
        STA networking. Rebuild with it disabled to restore the SDK timer table.

config APP_QUIET_UART
    bool "Silence logs and release UART TX after initialization"
    default n
    select LOG_SET_LEVEL
    help
        Keep startup diagnostics, then suppress ESP logs and configure GPIO1
        as an input. Rebuild with this disabled to restore runtime UART logs.

config APP_IDLE_BOOT_PINS
    bool "Release GPIO0 and GPIO15 after initialization"
    default y
    help
        Configure these boot strap pins as inputs without internal pulls.
        The board must provide its existing external boot strap resistors.

config APP_SENSOR_IDLE_INPUT
    bool "Release GPIO4 after temperature transactions"
    default y
    help
        Return the 1-Wire bus to input mode after initialization, failed
        conversion start and completed reads, including read failures.

endmenu

menu "Temperature calibration"

config APP_TEMP_OFFSET10
    int "DS18B20 temperature offset (0.1 C)"
    range -50 50
    default 0
    help
        Add this offset before rounding the raw temperature to 0.1 C.
        Use reference temperature minus sensor temperature after thermal
        equilibrium. Positive values raise the reading. Keep zero until
        a stable bias is measured; this cannot compensate changing heat sources.

endmenu
